// Plan 174.3 (D54 §6) — negative: `is` on a record operand is a compile error.
// The operand's type is statically known (a `User` record), so the runtime
// type-check is meaningless — `is` is legal only on `any` (v1) or sum-values (v2).
//
// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E_IS_NON_ANY

module neg.is_on_record
type User { id int }

fn bad(u User) -> bool => u is int
